> Quick comment: might be worth just waiting on https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/pull/4964?

@Rohan138  PR #4964 doesn't fix new head counts in general. It adds support for one more count, 96 heads, and fixes the existing workaround for unsupported counts. A new head count (lets say we got model with 112 heads) either runs a slow "folded" version of that kernel, or crashes(fallbacks to triton?) if it is not divisible by 16.

I'm proposing we have a universal padding so a new head count run with efficient kernel before we have a native support for it in aiter. The issue we've discussed today with @dllehr-amd, currently in this implementation I've tried to hard code what aiter is currently supporting which is not a good design. Would be easier to have a function that returns if there is a native support for the shape in aiter and if not what is the closes size to pad to.

